From: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi7: fix incomplete SAE struct types in sec_cmm.h

SECURITY_CONFIG embeds struct pwd_id_list and struct sae_capability
under "#if defined(DOT11_SAE_SUPPORT) || defined(SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT)",
but sec_cmm.h only includes security/sae_cmm.h (where those structs
are defined) under "#ifdef SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT".

With CONFIG_MTK_WIFI7_CFG80211_SUPPORT=y the vendor build defines
RT_CFG80211_SUPPORT, which makes owe_cmm.h skip its sae_cmm.h include
(it is guarded by "#ifndef RT_CFG80211_SUPPORT"). With
APCLI_SUPPLICANT_SUPPORT left off, SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT is never defined
either, so the SAE structs are not visible when the fields are
compiled and every TU pulling in sec_cmm.h fails with:

  error: field 'pwd_id_list_head' has incomplete type
  error: field 'sae_cap' has incomplete type

Match the include guard to the field guard so the struct definitions
are always present when the fields are compiled. link_list.h is pulled
in as well since struct pwd_id_list embeds a DL_LIST.

diff --git a/mt_wifi/include/common/security/sec_cmm.h b/mt_wifi/include/common/security/sec_cmm.h
index 872ec33..f3fbf23 100644
--- a/mt_wifi/include/common/security/sec_cmm.h
+++ b/mt_wifi/include/common/security/sec_cmm.h
@@ -12,7 +12,8 @@
 
 #include "security/owe_cmm.h"
 
-#ifdef SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT
+#if defined(DOT11_SAE_SUPPORT) || defined(SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT)
+#include "common/link_list.h"
 #include "security/sae_cmm.h"
 #endif
 
